    {
     "id": "7df1fba8-112f-4d91-b1bb-c4387bdeda2f",
     "prompt": "An iteration is $x_{n+1}=\\frac{7-x_n^2}{3}$. If it converges to a fixed point, which equation does the fixed point solve?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$x^2+3x-7=0$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$x^2-3x+7=0$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$x^2+3x+7=0$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$x^2-3x-7=0$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "At a fixed point, set $x_{n+1}=x_n=x$. Then $x=\\frac{7-x^2}{3}$, so $3x=7-x^2$ and therefore $x^2+3x-7=0$."
    },
    {
